    <section class="section">
      <div class="container two-col">
        <div class="prose">
          <h2>Built for tradespeople and small businesses</h2>
          <p>When a car breaks down it's an inconvenience. When a van breaks down, it's often a day's earnings or a missed job. We understand that a van being off the road affects your work, not just your commute, so the aim is always to get the vehicle collected and moved on with as little disruption as possible.</p>
          <p>This covers panel vans, small tradesperson's vans and other light commercial vehicles used for work. If you're driving a standard car rather than a van, our general <a href="car-recovery-aberdeen.html">car recovery</a> page is likely a better fit, and if you'd like the wider picture across every vehicle type we handle, see <a href="vehicle-recovery-aberdeen.html">vehicle recovery</a>.</p>

          <h2>Recovery to the destination that suits you</h2>
          <p>Rather than defaulting to a single depot, we'll take your van wherever you need it — your regular garage, a dealership, your own premises, or storage. Tell us the address when you call and that's where the van goes, so you can keep working with people you already trust rather than starting again with someone unfamiliar.</p>

          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Recovery of vans and light commercial vehicles.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Taken to a garage, depot or address of your choice.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Handled with tools, equipment or stock left inside.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> A single point of contact throughout the recovery.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>A word on contents.</strong> If your van is carrying tools, stock or equipment, we'll recover it as it stands, but we'd recommend removing anything particularly valuable or easily lost before we arrive if you're able to. We can't be responsible for loose items during transport, so it's worth a quick check if you have the time.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>When you need us</h2>
          <p>Whether it's a mechanical fault, a flat battery that won't take a jump, or a van that simply won't start on a job site, get in touch and describe the situation. We'll talk through where the van is, where it needs to go, and get a recovery vehicle moving.</p>
        </div>

