        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Can you recover a van with tools or stock inside?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>Yes, the van is recovered as it is. We'd recommend removing anything particularly valuable or easily lost beforehand if you're able to, simply because we can't be responsible for loose contents during transport.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Do you recover larger panel vans as well as small ones?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>We handle a range of van sizes. Tell us the make, model and roughly how large or heavily loaded the van is when you call, so we can confirm suitability and send the right equipment.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Can you take my van straight to my usual garage?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>Yes. Just give us the address when you call and we'll take the van there directly, rather than to a default location, so you can keep working with the garage you already trust.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
